Encoding.Description:
Local and global data share operations.

Examples:

    // Write 1 dword from v22 into LDS at byte address v12
    ds_write_b32 v12, v22
    // Read 1 dword from LDS byte address (v3 + 120), write value to v2
    ds_read_b32 v2, v3 offset:120
    // Write 2 dwords from v[4:5] into GDS at byte address v10
    ds_write_b32 v10, v[4:5] gds

Graphics export operations.

Example:

    // Export RGBA color to render target 0, using values in v[0:3]
    exp mrt0, v0, v1, v2, v3
    ...
    // Need to ensure the export has completed before modifying v0:
    s_waitcnt expcnt(0)
    v_mov_b32 v0, ...
    ...
    // Export a single colour to render target 1, and export the valid mask
    // Mark this as the final render target export with the 'done' flag:
    exp mrt1, v0, off, off, off done vm
